--- collections — length-indexed vectors, lists, and optionals on the
--- phase-3 unified type system.
---
--- Dogfood module for ADR-0106/0152/0153/0154: indexed `data` families,
--- implicit `<…>` index binders, dependent `match` elimination,
--- `Sigma`-encoded existentials, `IO<sig>` effect signatures, and
--- `instance` evidence. Written as a real library, not a test sketch.
---
--- Verified surface (`hnl typecheck src/collections.hnl` — clean):
---
---   data Maybe(a) :: Nothing | Just(x : a)
---   data Nat :: Zero | Succ(pred : Nat)
---   data Vec(n : Nat, a : Type) :: VNil : Vec(0, a)
---                                 | VCons(x : a, xs : Vec(n, a)) : Vec(n + 1, a)
---   data List(a : Type) :: LNil | LCons(h : a, t : List(a))
---
--- KNOWN GAPS (see /tmp/dogfood-report.md + host/project/design/
--- phase3-typesystem-spec.md progress log for the full writeup):
---
---   * The GADT-style declaration `VCons(k : Nat, x : a, xs : Vec(k, a))`
---     parses but the un-annotated result index is UNSOUND: `VCons`
---     synthesizes `Vec(?m, a)` with a free meta, so
---     `VCons(Zero, true, VNil) : Vec(5, Bool)` typechecks. Write the
---     result index explicitly — `VCons(x : a, xs : Vec(n, a)) : Vec(n + 1, a)`.
---   * FIXED — `append<n, m, a>` now typechecks: commuted sums with
---     rigid/meta atoms canonicalize (`?k + 1 + m ≡ m + ?k + 1`) —
---     unsolved metas are honest ring atoms in `poly_of`.
---   * FIXED — implicit-binder names scope into body annotations:
---     `(v : Vec(n, a))` under `f<n, a>` reads `n`/`a` as rigid index
---     vars, not unsolved sort metas.
---   * FIXED — `F.rec` is visible to the checker: `field_access` on a
---     `data` family resolves the `<F>.rec` scope binding; the
---     eliminator checks `motive ~> c0.. ~> indices.. ~> F ~> ?mo`.
---   * FIXED — `zipWith`'s catch-22 is gone: a decided-impossible arm
---     now *auto-discharges* (coverage never required it, `absurd` not
---     needed — it stays legal as documentation), so `match ys {
---     VNil: _, VCons(y, u): … }` under `n ≡ ?k + 1` typechecks.
---   * FIXED — `filter`'s existential output index: the Sigma
---     destructure now binds the witness rigidly (`var{m}` in both
---     results and Γ), and `unify_index`'s same-op `Bin` congruence
---     solves `?k + 1 ≡ var{m} + 1` — the recursive repack below
---     checks. There is still no `?m`/`∃` surface (`Vec<?m, a>`
---     fails to lex); `exists m. T` sugar remains BACKLOG'd.
---   * `T.rec` — NOW CHECKED (`hnl typecheck` accepts
---     `Vec.rec(null, 0, step)(2, Bool, v)`); `match` is still the
---     elimination form used below.
---   * Recursion typechecks AND runs correctly on the tree-walk
---     AST-eval path (`vsum` → `Succ` tower; `toNum ∘ vsum → 2`) —
---     bytecode/cranelift still diverge on self-recursive closures
---     (remaining issue). Previously it ran WRONG: `vmap`/`vsum` below check
---     cleanly and `hnl run` evaluates them — silently producing the
---     wrong value (`vmap` returns the input unchanged; `vsum` returns
---     `Zero`). `lower_ast` rejects self-recursive calls ("the arrow
---     calculus has no recursion") and the AST-eval fallback computes
---     incorrect results on all three engines. `rec {…}(…)` cannot
---     express self-recursive functions from the surface either (assign
---     syntax rejected inside the region; object-literal state fields
---     aren't scope-bound for the body).
---   * Runtime `match` on a *parameterized* family needs BOTH an
---     annotated scrutinee `match (v : Fam(i⃗)) {…}` AND all-ctor
---     coverage to desugar to `F.rec`; otherwise it silently
---     misdispatches — a bare `VNil:`/`Nope:` pattern acts as a catch-all
---     binder (verified: `match Jx(9) { Jx(x): 111, Nope: 222 }` → 222).
---     But `(v : Vec(n, a))` annotations can't name `<n,a>`-bound
---     implicit index vars inside a body — the stored domain keeps
---     unsolved metas (`cannot unify — expected [?m1, ?m0], got [n, a]`),
---     and in paren annotations bare names read as sorts. So a
---     polymorphic function over `Vec<n, a>` can be checked OR run
---     correctly, not both.
---   * A constructor named `J` is unwritable — `J` is the J-eliminator
---     keyword; `data Opt :: N | J(x : a)` errors with the unhelpful
---     "expected separator token.comma" (no "reserved keyword" hint).

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Types
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------

Maybe<a> := {
  Nothing : Maybe,
  Just : (x : a) ~> Maybe
}

Nat := {
  Zero : Nat,
  Succ : (pred : Nat) ~> Nat
}

--- The length index is a Nat *sort* (literal/arithmetized) — `Succ`-form
--- indices (`Vec<Succ n, a>`) read through the WS-D ctor-projection
--- bridge and are definitionally `n + 1`.
Vec<n : Nat, a : Type> := {
  VNil : Vec(0, a),
  VCons : (x : a, xs : Vec(n, a)) ~> Vec(n + 1, a)
}

List<a : Type> := {
  LNil : List,
  LCons : (h : a, t : List(a)) ~> List
}

--- A small typeclass-shaped former + instance (WS-A): `Eq(a)` is a
--- nominal former; `instance Eq(Nat) := <dict>` registers a dictionary,
--- and an `<ev : Eq(a)>` implicit binder discharges by search. Members
--- are projected by matching the `mkEq` constructor out of the
--- dictionary — `ev.eq` field access does NOT typecheck (the binder's
--- type is the `Eq(a)` former-app, not a record — `record_field_type`
--- error), so `match ev { mkEq(f): … }` is the call convention.
Eq<a : Type> := {
  mkEq : (f : a ~> a ~> Bool) ~> Eq
}

instance Eq(Nat) := { eq: (x, y) ~> x == y }

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Vec — construction and safe access
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- A one-element vector. `1` in the index is the literal Nat sort.
export vsingleton<a> : a ~> Vec<1, a> = x ~> VCons(x, VNil)

--- `head` is total on non-empty vectors: `Vec<Succ n, a>` is
--- definitionally `Vec<n + 1, a>` (WS-D bridge), so the VCons-only
--- match is *provably* exhaustive — no catchall needed, and a stray
--- `VNil` arm is rejected as decided-unreachable (or discharged with
--- `VNil: absurd`). Typechecks AND runs (`hnl run` — single-arm match
--- takes the ctor-object dispatch path).
export vhead<n, a> : Vec<Succ n, a> ~> a = v ~> match v { VCons(x, xs): x }

export vtail<n, a> : Vec<n + 1, a> ~> Vec<n, a> = v ~> match v { VCons(x, xs): xs }

--- `vmap` TYPECHECKS the natural dependent form: implicit `<n, a, b>`
--- binders, `match` refinement (`xs : Vec<?k, a>` under VCons gives
--- `?k + 1 ≡ n`), and a self-recursive call. RUNTIME CAVEAT: the
--- self-call lowers as unsupported (arrow calculus has no recursion)
--- and the AST-eval fallback returns the input unchanged — see the gap
--- log. Kept because the *checking* contract is real.
export vmap<n, a, b> : (a ~> b) ~> Vec<n, a> ~> Vec<n, b> =
  f ~> v ~> match v {
    VNil: VNil,
    VCons(x, xs): VCons(f(x), vmap(f)(xs))
  }

--- Same check-vs-run split for a fold: `vsum` checks (VNil → Zero,
--- VCons → Succ of the recursive sum) but runs to `Zero`.
export vsum<n> : Vec<n, Nat> ~> Nat =
  v ~> match v { VNil: Zero, VCons(x, xs): Succ(vsum(xs)) }

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Maybe — total ops (parameterized family; see match caveats above)
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------

export mmap<a, b> : (a ~> b) ~> Maybe(a) ~> Maybe(b) =
  f ~> m ~> match m { Nothing: Nothing, Just(x): Just(f(x)) }

export mget<a> : Maybe(a) ~> a ~> a =
  m ~> d ~> match m { Nothing: d, Just(x): x }

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Vec — partial/filtered operations via the Sigma existential
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- `filter` can't name an output length — there is no `?m`/`∃` index
--- syntax — so the honest return is `Sigma(Nat, m ~> Vec(m, a))`: some
--- `m` with a `Vec(m, a)`. The Sigma intro is the `[witness, value]`
--- pair (`[Zero, VNil]`); the eliminator `match s { [m, ys]: … }`
--- binds `m` as a rigid index var (`var{m}`) and `ys` at
--- `Vec(var{m}, a)`, so the repack `[Succ(m), VCons(x, ys)]` solves
--- `?k := var{m}` in `Vec(?k + 1, a) ≡ Vec(m + 1, a)`.
export filter<n, a> : (a ~> Bool) ~> Vec<n, a> ~> Sigma(Nat, m ~> Vec(m, a)) =
  f ~> v ~> match v {
    VNil: [Zero, VNil],
    VCons(x, xs): match filter(f)(xs) {
      [m, ys]: if f(x) { [Succ(m), VCons(x, ys)] } else { [m, ys] }
    }
  }

--- Length-agreeing zip. The inner `match ys`'s `VNil` arm is
--- decided-impossible under the outer `VCons` refinement (`n ≡ ?k + 1`,
--- `?k` a Nat-sorted meta) — auto-discharged: the body below is
--- unchecked-but-allowed (`absurd` remains legal documentation).
--- RUNTIME CAVEAT: same check-vs-run split as `vmap`/`vsum` — the
--- self-recursive call checks cleanly but the tree-walk eval can't
--- apply it correctly today.
export zipWith<n, a, b, c> : (a ~> b ~> c) ~> Vec<n, a> ~> Vec<n, b> ~> Vec<n, c> =
  f ~> xs ~> ys ~> match xs {
    VNil: VNil,
    VCons(x, t): match ys { VNil: VNil, VCons(y, u): VCons(f(x)(y), zipWith(f)(t)(u)) }
  }

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Evidence — instance resolution in the implicit-binder slot
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- `<ev : Eq(a)>` discharges by dictionary search at the call site —
--- `eqv(Zero)` resolves the `Eq(Nat)` instance with no explicit dict
--- argument. The dict's method is reached by matching `mkEq(f)` — see
--- the `Eq` comment above for why `ev.eq` doesn't work.
export eqv<a, ev : Eq(a)> : a ~> a ~> Bool = x ~> y ~> match ev { mkEq(f): f(x, y) }

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Effects — IO<sig> signatures (ADR-0153 §4)
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- Effect signatures as annotations. There is no `declare`/`extern`
--- form — a signature-only operation still needs a body, so these are
--- self-referencing stubs (they typecheck; applying them diverges).
--- A `builtin`/`extern` surface for op declarations is a phase-4 item.
export readFile : Str ~> IO<{ fs }> = p ~> readFile(p)
export printLn : Str ~> IO<{ puts }> = s ~> printLn(s)

--- Handling discharges ops: a covering impl replaces the op's sig entry
--- with the impl's return type (`IO<{ puts: Unit }>` — `puts` is handled,
--- nothing residual). Check-side only: calling the stubs diverges.
puts_handler : (Str ~> Unit) ~> Unit = req ~> req("handled")
handled_printLn : Str ~> IO<{ puts: Unit }> = handle printLn with { puts: puts_handler }

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- forall — explicit-Pi alias (type-level quantification)
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- `Forall(K, x ~> B)` is the explicit-Pi spelling; `forall a. …`
--- dot-syntax does NOT parse (phase-4 sugar candidate).
export forall_id : Forall(Nat, n ~> Nat) = n ~> n

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fails-to-write (documented in the header comment; kept as text so the
--- gate file stays clean)
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
--   append<n, m, a> : Vec<n, a> ~> Vec<m, a> ~> Vec<n + m, a> =
--     xs ~> ys ~> match xs { VNil: ys, VCons(x, t): VCons(x, append(t)(ys)) }
--   -- cannot unify — expected Vec(m + ?m9 + 1, ?m11), got Vec(m + ?m9 + 1, ?m11)
--   -- (with return motive: expected Vec(?m9 + 1 + m, ?m0), got Vec(m + ?m9 + 1, ?m11))
--
--   -- (zipWith now lives above — auto-discharge removed the catch-22.)
--
--   filter<a> : (a ~> Bool) ~> Vec<n, a> ~> Vec<?m, a>   -- `?m` doesn't lex
--   Vec.rec(null, z, s)(n, a, v)                        -- `record_field_type` error
--   data Vec(n : Nat, a : Type) :: VNil | VCons(k : Nat, x : a, xs : Vec(k, a))
--                                                     -- un-annotated result index is unsound

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Runnable smoke (typechecked above; `hnl run` prints the last binding).
-- Only statements verified to evaluate *correctly* are here: `vhead`/
-- `vtail` take the single-arm ctor-object dispatch path. `mmap`/`mget`
-- run but silently take the wrong arm (unannotated parameterized-family
-- match — see header); `eqv` matches a dict that carries no `__ctor__`;
-- the IO stubs diverge. All check-side clean.
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------

smoke_vec : Vec<2, Bool> = VCons(true, VCons(false, VNil))
smoke_head : Bool = vhead(smoke_vec)
smoke_tail : Vec<1, Bool> = vtail(smoke_vec)
